WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.370
- Hi, I'm Catherine McCord

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.420
and today on Pro Tips from Pro Chefs,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.340
I'm gonna be showing you road trip snacks

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.050
that are gonna save you as
you head on your destination

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.730
and make sure that your bellies are full.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.150
- Something we already know,
America loves road trips.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.560
- Oh, can we talk about road trip snacks?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.143
(lively music)

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.650
- One of our favorite travel recipes

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.160
are these cucumber stackers.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.780
They're also perfect
if you are gluten free,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.290
'cause there's no bread in them.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.450
So you can take a cucumber,

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.690
Persian or English
cucumber, whatever you like.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.500
You can keep the skin on or skin off.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.690
I like the skin on,
especially with the Persians,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.410
because they are much thinner
than an English cucumber.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.940
And you wanna cut them
about a half an inch

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.640
and just remember, this is your bread.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.550
Not exactly the bread
that you might be used to

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.660
but it gives a little bit of crunch

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.560
and you get a vegetable in there too.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.500
Then we're gonna take some
cheese and some turkey.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.410
So you can put 'em side by
side, on top of each other,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.660
whatever you like.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.840
Now is the fun part, cookie cutters.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.540
They are not just for Christmas.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.380
I use them all year round in
different kinds of shapes.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.440
These are kind of flowers
and clouds and stars,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.010
but again, use what you've got.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:22.010
So I just take them like this, super fun.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.830
You can get your kids involved if you want

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.950
'cause it's a really fun one.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.890
All right, and again,
like different shapes.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.170
And when they're eating
them, you can have them say,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.760
like, what kind of shape
do you think is in there?

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.160
Because on a long trip,
you wanna keep everyone

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.770
as entertained as possible.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.370
Okay, so you're gonna put a cucumber

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.920
and put your star on top

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.250
and then you can just place
them right on top like that.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.310
And you can use other
kinds of deli meat too.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.450
You could use ham, pastrami, roast beef.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.710
Same thing goes with the cheese.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.190
I like to use cheddar
but you could also use

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:59.190
mozzarella, Colby, muenster,
Swiss, anything you enjoy.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.980
All right, so I've got my turkey

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.740
and I'm just gonna put
my cheese right on top.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.340
All you do is put the
cucumber right on top

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.690
and that is a cucumber stacker,
only three ingredients.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.600
The perfect bite size treat

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:23.230
to get a vegetable in there
and protein as you're traveling

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.580
and make sure that no one
gets hangry on your road trip.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.400
And don't forget, if you
have scraps like this,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.900
feel free to throw 'em in a sandwich now

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.233
and keep your cucumber stackers for later.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.000
Peanut butter and jelly
sandwiches are totally yesterday.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.240
I am talking about peanut
butter and jelly pop tarts.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.540
These are homemade,
only three ingredients.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.790
You need pie crust, that
you can make yourself

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:49.950
or you can buy prepared

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.760
in the refrigerator
section of your grocery.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.280
And then I just fill them,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.400
these little squares about
two inches by three inches,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.200
with a teaspoon of peanut
butter, a teaspoon of jelly.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.500
You bake them up in a 400 degree oven

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.540
until they're nice and golden like this.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.820
Now, the fun part though,
comes with the glaze.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.870
So I like to put one on a surface

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.880
and then I've got a little
bit of powdered sugar here.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.410
After all, you're on a road trip

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.970
and it's all about making
it as fun as possible.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.340
So in the powdered sugar, I
like to put some food color

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.940
and then you're gonna
just add in a little milk.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.480
Now you wanna do this
a little bit at a time

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.260
because we're just trying to
make a really beautiful glaze.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.290
And ask your kids what color they want.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.660
Blue, green, yellow,

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.890
they can play with their primary colors.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.980
All right, just slowly stir, stir, stir,

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:44.430
adding just a little bit
of that milk at a time

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.350
'cause you wanna make sure that
your glaze is thick enough.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.420
You don't want it to be too runny.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:50.750
All right, so stir it.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.813
Ooh yes, that's what we're talking about.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.763
Look at that pretty, pretty color.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.350
And you just want it like
that kind of a consistency.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:05.360
Just thick enough, but
spreadable at the same time.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.457
And then we're just gonna
put a little of that glaze.

00:04:07.457 --> 00:04:11.460
Let it drip, drip, drip so
it doesn't make a big mess

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.870
and then we're just gonna
spread it right on it.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.440
Like to use a spoon
'cause it makes it easier

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.830
just to spread it all around.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:23.260
And just that extra
bit of sweetness on top

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:27.570
makes it fun to look at,
but also to enjoy tasting.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.860
And then, just to really up the ante,

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.010
I like to put some sprinkles on top.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.010
Just a few to give it a little pop.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.200
Look how cute those are.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.123
They're like the perfect summertime treat.

00:04:40.123 --> 00:04:42.706
(upbeat music)

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.730
At any given time, I have four
boxes of cereal in my pantry

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:49.850
with just about this much leftover.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.270
So these cereal bars are the perfect use

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.400
for that kind of leftover cereal.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.160
I dump them in, I add
a ton of peanut butter

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.950
or any kind of nut or
seed butter that you like,

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:04.030
a little bit of coconut oil,
which is the greatest tip

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.340
kind of keeping them together,

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.810
and then some oats so that you get

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.570
that whole grain goodness.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:13.040
I put everything into this
nine by nine inch pan.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.140
Always line your pans with
parchment paper, just like this.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.550
That way, they pull right out.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.570
It makes clean up and
cutting them a breeze.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:27.090
So just take that parchment
and then take a serrated knife

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.820
and we're just gonna cut them like this.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.620
Another great tip is if you feel like

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.847
you need to head out on your road trip

00:05:33.847 --> 00:05:36.130
and you wanna make these really fast,

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.310
just put 'em in the freezer

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.520
'cause they'll set up really quick.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.123
And then we can just turn,
turn, turn and cut them.

00:05:46.046 --> 00:05:48.120
Ugh, look at that.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:52.730
Not only are they absolutely
delicious, but look at that.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.330
Any kind of cereal you like is gonna work

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.780
for these on the go bars.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.120
I don't know many kids
who don't love cereal

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.770
but who wants to take milk with
their cereal on a road trip?

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:05.170
These cereal bars are a ton more fun,

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:09.490
have a lot of protein
in them, and no mess.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.920
Last but definitely not least
is my super healthy granola.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.470
I have a batch of this
with me at all times.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:23.180
Why? Because it is like hearty,
you can put it in parfaits.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:27.460
I'm gonna tell you my tip
for getting these huge chunks

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.050
that look more like granola
bars than they do granola.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.240
So after you add in all
of your ingredients,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.760
you're gonna allow it to spread out,

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.880
bake it in a 250 degree oven

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.940
for about an hour and 45 minutes,

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.840
take it out and totally let it cool

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.590
because that cooling
process allows it to get

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.060
nice and crispy, stick together.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:52.920
So when it comes out of the
oven, it's in these huge chunks,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.280
you can break into smaller
pieces, put in a bag.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.860
And that, for me, is the
best on the go snack.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.230
The reason I love this
granola and making it,

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.590
it's so much better than store bought.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.700
You can control the ingredients in here.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.900
You get a lot more bang for your buck

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.750
and it's not too sweet.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.820
There's no refined sweeteners in it.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.223
So it's just that perfect
kiss in every single bite.

